# Tenant data is per-org and per-environment

Tenants (Taste of Andhra, Spice Malabar, others) **must not share** menus, categories, orders, customers-at-restaurant, or settings. All of those are scoped by `organization_id`.

## Storefront isolation (every restaurant host)

Each `{slug}.directapp.in` (and custom domain) is a **separate restaurant**. Do not send customers to Taste of Andhra URLs, copy, UPI IDs, or login helpers.

- Checkout, cart, payment links, invoices, and OAuth redirects stay on `window.location.origin` of the current host.
- Never fall back to `APP_NAME`, `thetasteofandhra.com`, or Taste of Andhra UPI (`tasteofandhra@okaxis`) for another tenant. Use `restaurantDisplayName` / org settings (`src/utils/tenantFeatures.ts`).
- Optional features are **per org**. WhatsApp click-to-order is **off by default** for new restaurants (including Spice Malabar). Restaurant admin enables it in Admin → Settings (`organizations.settings.storefront_whatsapp_enabled`).
- Onboarding a new restaurant: copy the light storefront (menu, cart, checkout, login) on that subdomain; do not link to another tenant. Seed `storefront_whatsapp_enabled: false` unless the owner asked for WhatsApp.

## Two databases

| Env | Project | Typical access |
|-----|---------|----------------|
| Local / staging | `zsfjpapatepmnbtxvvaw` (`taste-of-andhra-staging`) | `.env.local` |
| Production | `qixpsqlifwsztncjevgl` (`taste-of-andhra`) | Vercel `VITE_SUPABASE_*` |

Pushing the frontend **does not** copy tenant rows. A tenant that works locally can show “Menu coming soon” on `{slug}.directapp.in` if production was never seeded.

## When adding or changing a tenant

1. Seed/onboard against **staging** first (`npm run seed:spice-malabar` with `.env.local`).
2. Then seed **production**: `npm run seed:spice-malabar:production` (or `scripts/seed-production.mjs <seed-file>`).
3. Confirm production: org row for the slug, plus dish/category counts for that `organization_id`.
4. Require `VITE_ENABLE_HOST_TENANT_RESOLUTION=true` on Vercel Production; otherwise every host falls back to Taste of Andhra.

Symptom: tenant branding on `https://{slug}.directapp.in` + empty menu → org resolved, **prod catalog missing**. See `docs/PRODUCTION_TENANT_SETUP.md`.

Spice Malabar public URL is `https://chopsticksspicemalabar.directapp.in`. Do not serve or alias `spice-malabar.directapp.in` (retired; remove from DNS later). Do not use `www.{slug}.directapp.in` — wildcard DNS does not cover it.
